619/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1369506410c49b01082ee2534bb5d81132c4ee1841950af3916c6fe046d1eb6"} {"question" "q-69623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $G+H-(H+F)$, if\n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,G=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,H=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977619/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1369506410c49b01082ee2534bb5d81132c4ee1841950af3916c6fe046d1eb6"} {"question" "q-69623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G+H-(H+F) & =G+H-H-F \\\\  & =G+\\cancel{H}-\\cancel{H}-F \\\\  & =G-F\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single subtraction. So, we subtract the corresponding entries of the two matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G-F & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5-2 & 4-(-1) & -5-2 \\\\ 1-3 & -2-4 & 2-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & -7 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977619/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1369506410c49b01082ee2534bb5d81132c4ee1841950af3916c6fe046d1eb6"} {"question" "q-69623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977619/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a4005e4a89523fa760e8794a08ecab5d054df6b3638eb6da719e4d0092ffb05b"} {"question" "q-69623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/ho