 & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single matrix. So, the result is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977619/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1369506410c49b01082ee2534bb5d81132c4ee1841950af3916c6fe046d1eb6"} {"question" "q-13536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977619/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a4005e4a89523fa760e8794a08ecab5d054df6b3638eb6da719e4d0092ffb05b"} {"question" "q-13536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977619/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1369506410c49b01082ee2534bb5d81132c4ee1841950af3916c6fe046d1eb6"} {"question" "q-13536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977619/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1369506410c49b01082ee2534bb5d81132c4ee1841950af3916c6fe046d1eb6"} {"question" "q-13536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977619/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1369506410c49b01082ee2534bb5d81132c4ee1841950af3916c6fe046d1eb6"} {"question" "q-69627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $C+V-(N+C)$, if\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}10 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 25 \\\\ -57 & -23\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -8\\end{aligned}],\\,N=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -7 \\\\ 2 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977619/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1369506410c49b01082ee2534bb5d81132c4ee1841950af3916c6fe046d1eb6"} {"question" "q-69627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C+V-(N+C) & =C+V-N-C \\\\  & =\\cancel{C}+V-N-\\cancel{C} \\\\  & =V-N\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single subtraction. So, we subtract the corresponding entries of the two matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V-N & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -8\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & -7 \\\\ 2 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5-1 & 3-(-7) \\\\ 6-2 & -4-(-6) \\\\ -1-3 & -8-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 10 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -13\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977619/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1369506410c49b01082ee2534bb5d81132c4ee1841950af3916c6fe046d1eb6"} {"question" "q-69627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977619/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a4005e4a89523fa760e8794a08ecab5d054df6b3638eb6da719e4d0092ffb05b"} {"question" "q-69627" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacad